course: dictionary
lesson: 9994
title: Teenage: a word about age
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: «Teenage brothers need space.» Teenage is an adjective, a describing word. It tells you about a person's age: between 13 and 19. A teenager is someone in that age range, and teenage is the word for it.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. In «my teenage brother», the word brother tells you who, and teenage tells you how old. In «teenage years», the word years tells you the time of life. To check, swap in a number: a 15-year-old is a teenager, so teenage fits.
explain: The word can also describe things connected with people of that age. «Teenage characters have adventures» means the characters in the story are of that age group. Teenage describes their age, so it can describe people or the things linked to them.
fact: Teenage means aged between 13 and 19, or connected with people of that age.
fact: «Teenage years» are the years from 13 to 19.
fact: Teenage is an adjective: it describes a noun, as in «teenage girl» or «teenage boy».
fact: «Children usually grow about 5 to 6 centimetres a year, faster as babies and again during the teenage years.»
fact: Growth plates are bands of soft cartilage near the ends of bones, and they close into solid bone when the teenage years end.
exercise: «Teenage brothers need space.» How old are teenage brothers? | Aged between 1 and 5 | Aged 60 and over | *Aged between 13 and 19
exercise: «Joan of Arc, a teenage peasant girl, led the French to victory.» What does teenage mean here? | Very tall and strong | Rich and famous | *Of the age of 13 to 19 | Very old and wise
exercise: «Young famous people, like teenage TV actors, deserve even more privacy.» Which word describes the actors? | privacy | *teenage | actors | TV
test: Ella is 14 years old. Which word could describe her? | Famished | Luminous | Curt | *Teenage
test: Teenage means which of these? | *Between 13 and 19 years old | Very quiet, like a whisper | Only a baby | Between 30 and 40 years old
exam: «Growth plates close into solid bone when the teenage years end.» What do the teenage years mean in this sentence? | The years after you turn 60 | *The years from 13 to 19 | The years when you are very old | The years when you are a baby
